# Backend API layer (`src/api/`)

## Purpose

- **HTTP-agnostic logic** in `src/services/` (shared with legacy) and **`src/api/services/`** for v1-specific orchestration when needed.
- **HTTP adapters** only in **`src/api/http/*.http.ts`** (and `registerApiV1Routes.ts`): parse/validate requests, call services, map status + **v1 JSON envelope**.
- **Legacy** route files stay in `src/routes/` and stay thin; they delegate to the same services as v1 where migrated.
- **Catalog (DBV lists + foil map):** **`/api/v1/catalog/*`** in **`dbv-catalog.http.ts`** → **`CatalogService`** only. Handlers do **not** touch **`CardRepository`** / **`FoilCardMapRepository`** directly—those are wired only into **`CatalogService`** in the composition root.

## Documentation (mandatory)

- **Legacy** contract: [API_DOCUMENTATION.md](../../API_DOCUMENTATION.md)
- **v1** contract: [API_V1.md](../../API_V1.md) — sole place for `/api/v1` paths, examples, `{ data, meta, errors }`.
- **Migration progress:** [API_MIGRATION_CHECKLIST.md](../../API_MIGRATION_CHECKLIST.md)
- **Architecture narrative:** [MIGRATION_ARCHITECTURE.md](../../MIGRATION_ARCHITECTURE.md)
- Agent workflow: [.cursor/skills/api-layer-migration/SKILL.md](../../.cursor/skills/api-layer-migration/SKILL.md)

Any change to a **published HTTP contract** must update the right doc(s) in the **same** change.

## Layering (v1 + migrations)

| Layer | Responsibility | Forbidden |
|-------|----------------|-----------|
| **`*.http.ts`** | Routing, validate → **request models**, call **one** service method, v1 envelope | Business rules, direct DB/repository calls, defining request/response types inline as source of truth |
| **Services** | Business logic; **admin-only** work behind **admin-scoped** entry points only used from `/api/v1/admin/...` | `req`/`res`; branching on **client-supplied** admin/role flags |
| **Repositories** | Persistence | HTTP |
| **Request models** | One **file** per body/query/param contract | Ad hoc `req.body` typing in routes only |
| **Response DTOs** | One **file** per public response shape | Anonymous-only public responses in routes |

## Admin namespace

- Elevated operations only under **`/api/v1/admin/...`**.
- No `isAdmin` / `role` / `elevated` in request bodies to select privileged code paths.
- Non-`/admin` routes **must not** call admin-privileged service methods.

## Passwords / hashing

- **Do not** change password hashing, bcrypt cost, or stored credentials as part of API work.
- v1 login uses **`AuthenticationService.authenticateUser`** (same stack as cookie login); JWT is **after** successful verify.

## Security

- Cross-cutting: middleware (Bearer JWT, rate limits, role checks), not duplicated ad hoc in every handler.
- **JWT:** `JWT_SECRET` required when `NODE_ENV=production`. `JWT_ACCESS_TTL` (default `15m`) and `JWT_REFRESH_TTL_SECONDS` (default 30 days) from Phase 2. See [MIGRATION_ARCHITECTURE.md](../../MIGRATION_ARCHITECTURE.md) and [docs/current/API_V1_AUTH_REFRESH.md](../../docs/current/API_V1_AUTH_REFRESH.md).
- **Refresh tokens:** issued/rotated/revoked by [`services/refreshTokenService.ts`](services/refreshTokenService.ts); backed by `refresh_tokens` table ([`migrations/V275__Create_refresh_tokens.sql`](../../migrations/V275__Create_refresh_tokens.sql)). Kill switch `DISABLE_AUTH_REFRESH=1` ([docs/current/API_V1_AUTH_REFRESH.md](../../docs/current/API_V1_AUTH_REFRESH.md)).
- **Audit log:** every `/api/v1/*` request async-writes a row into `api_access_log` via [`http/middleware/apiAccessLog.ts`](http/middleware/apiAccessLog.ts); 90-day retention ([docs/current/API_V1_AUDIT_LOG.md](../../docs/current/API_V1_AUDIT_LOG.md)). Kill switch `DISABLE_API_ACCESS_LOG=1`.
- **Rate limits:** consolidated in [`http/middleware/v1RateLimit.ts`](http/middleware/v1RateLimit.ts); `X-RateLimit-*` headers + 429 with `RATE_LIMITED` ([docs/current/API_V1_RATE_LIMITS.md](../../docs/current/API_V1_RATE_LIMITS.md)). Kill switches `DISABLE_V1_RATE_LIMIT=1` / `LEGACY_RATE_LIMITS=1`.
- **Body validation:** every `*.http.ts` mutation body goes through [`parseV1Body`](http/parseV1Body.ts) (zod) ([docs/current/API_V1_VALIDATION.md](../../docs/current/API_V1_VALIDATION.md)). Kill switch `DISABLE_ZOD_V1=1`.
- **Decks + collections auth:** session cookie OR Bearer JWT via `createV1SessionOrBearerAuthMiddleware`. Kill switch `DISABLE_BEARER_DECKS_COLLECTIONS=1` restores session-only (pre-Phase-2).
- **Catalog caching:** `/api/v1/catalog/*` and `/api/v1/dbv/sets` go through [`http/catalogCache.ts`](http/catalogCache.ts) which emits `Cache-Control`, strong `ETag`, and `meta.catalogDataVersion`; honors `If-None-Match`; optional `?since_version=<n>`. CloudFront ordered cache behaviors in [`infra/cloudfront.tf`](../../infra/cloudfront.tf). Kill switches `DISABLE_CATALOG_CACHE_HEADERS=1` / `DISABLE_SINCE_SYNC=1` ([docs/current/API_V1_CATALOG_CACHING.md](../../docs/current/API_V1_CATALOG_CACHING.md)).
- **Error catalog + OpenAPI (contract):** any new `/api/v1` route MUST add an entry in [docs/current/API_V1_ERROR_CATALOG.md](../../docs/current/API_V1_ERROR_CATALOG.md), a path in [docs/openapi.yaml](../../docs/openapi.yaml), and a line in [docs/current/API_V1_CHANGELOG.md](../../docs/current/API_V1_CHANGELOG.md) — all in the same PR as the route.
- **Image URL contract:** external clients consume images from `APP_CDN_BASE` via the paths defined in [docs/current/API_V1_IMAGE_CONTRACT.md](../../docs/current/API_V1_IMAGE_CONTRACT.md). Do not introduce new image path shapes without updating that doc.

## Testing (mandatory)

- **Unit:** all service + DTO logic; **full** unit coverage per `src/api/http/*.http.ts` (every route + main error branches).
- **Integration:** **≥1** integration test per `*.http.ts` (Supertest + real app wiring).
- Do not commit without relevant tests passing (`npm run test:unit`; integration when routes are user-visible).

## Imports

- **Never** import from `public/` or frontend bundles into `src/api/`.

## Route grouping (`src/api/http/`)

1. `auth.http.ts` — login, logout, me.
2. `dbv-catalog.http.ts` — card catalog reads for DBV.
3. `dbv-support.http.ts` — DBV reference reads (`/dbv/sets`, `/dbv/deck-backgrounds` with session auth).
4. `recent-updates.http.ts` — Home screen news cards (`GET /recent-updates`, `RecentUpdatesService`; session-or-Bearer auth).
5. `decks.http.ts` — user decks: list (`GET /decks`, `DeckListService`); community pool (`GET /decks/community`, `community_decks` user, `updated_at` desc); tournament pool (`GET /decks/tournament`, `tournament_decks` user, `updated_at` desc); aggregate stats (`GET /decks/stats`, `DeckStatsService`); create/validate (`DeckWriteService`); single deck read/update/delete and `/decks/:id/full` (`DeckDetailService`, `UpdateDeckRequestBody`); deck cards (`GET`/`POST`/`PUT`/`DELETE /decks/:id/cards`, `DeckCardsService`, `DeckCardsPostBody` / `DeckCardsPutBody`); UI preferences (`/decks/:id/ui-preferences`, `DeckUIPreferencesService`). Session auth (same `authenticateUser` as other DB deck routes). Register `/decks/community` and `/decks/tournament` **before** `/decks/:id`.
6. `guest-decks.http.ts` — **`/guest/decks...`** (`GuestDeckService`, GUEST + `sessionId` cookie).
7. `collections.http.ts` — **`/collections/me...`** (`CollectionService`, session auth).
8. `saved-database-views.http.ts` — personal **`/saved-database-views...`** CRUD and bulk delete (`SavedDatabaseViewService`, session-or-Bearer auth, centralized temporary ADMIN eligibility policy). This is intentionally outside `/admin` because records are always current-user-owned; the policy is replaceable by the Supporter entitlement service.
9. `admin.http.ts` — **`/admin/users`**, **`/admin/user-analytics`**, **`/admin/biz-ops-dashboard`**, **`/admin/debug/*`**, **`/admin/database/status`** (`AdminService` / `AdminBizOpsDashboardService`, session + **ADMIN**).
10. `users.http.ts` — **`/users/change-email`**, **`/users/change-password`** (`UserAccountService`, session + USER/ADMIN).

Register via **`registerApiV1Routes`** in `registerApiV1Routes.ts`.

## Endpoint hit metrics

- New **`/api/v1/...`** routes added in `*.http.ts` and mounted through **`registerApiV1Routes`** are included in **`enumerateExpressRoutes`** at server startup and get a **`endpoint_hit_counts` row at zero** (plus runtime upsert on first hit). **Removed** Express routes are dropped from the table on the next startup via **`pruneStaleEndpointHitCounts`**. No Flyway INSERT per route—see [`docs/current/ENDPOINT_HIT_METRICS.md`](../../docs/current/ENDPOINT_HIT_METRICS.md) and [`src/metrics/.cursorrules`](../metrics/.cursorrules).
